## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of two classic sorts, practical optimization, and memory trade-offs. A hybrid approach reveals ability to tune algorithms for real data patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Hybrid sorting threshold and when it helps
- Stability via merge vs insertion behavior
- Space usage with a single auxiliary buffer

## Code Example
```javascript
function sortBatch(arr) {
  const n = arr.length;
  const buf = new Array(n);
  function insertionSort(a, left, right) {
    for (let i = left + 1; i <= right; i++) {
      const key = a[i];
      let j = i - 1;
      while (j >= left && a[j] > key) {
        a[j + 1] = a[j];
        j--;
      }
      a[j + 1] = key;
    }
  }
  function merge(left, mid, right) {
    let i = left, j = mid + 1, k = left;
    while (i <= mid && j <= right) {
      if (arr[i] <= arr[j]) buf[k++] = arr[i++];
      else buf[k++] = arr[j++];
    }
    while (i <= mid) buf[k++] = arr[i++];
    while (j <= right) buf[k++] = arr[j++];
    for (let t = left; t <= right; t++) arr[t] = buf[t];
  }
  function sort(l, r) {
    if (l >= r) return;
    if (r - l + 1 <= 16) {
      insertionSort(arr, l, r);
    } else {
      const m = Math.floor((l + r) / 2);
      sort(l, m);
      sort(m + 1, r);
      merge(l, m, r);
    }
  }
  sort(0, n - 1);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design augmented self-balancing BSTs for dynamic range queries—a common requirement in analytics and data processing applications.

## Key Concepts

- **AVL balancing**: Maintaining height balance factor (|left.height - right.height| ≤ 1) through rotations
- **Augmented BST data**: Storing additional aggregate information (cnt, sum) at each node
- **Range query on BST**: Using the BST property to efficiently prune irrelevant subtrees
- **Correctness and complexity analysis**: Ensuring O(log n) operations and verifying invariants

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(key) {
    this.key = key;
    this.cnt = 1;
    this.height = 1;
    this.left = null;
    this.right = null;
    this.sum = key;
  }
}

function getHeight(node) { return node ? node.height : 0; }
function getSum(node) { return node ? node.sum : 0; }
function update(node) {
  node.height = 1 + Math.max(getHeight(node.left), getHeight(node.right));
  node.sum = getSum(node.left) + node.key * node.cnt + getSum(node.right);
}

function rightRotate(y) {
  const x = y.left;
  y.left = x.right;
  x.right = y;
  update(y);
  update(x);
  return x;
}

function rangeSum(node, a, b) {
  if (!node) return 0;
  if (node.key < a) return rangeSum(node.right, a, b);
  if (node.key > b) return rangeSum(node.left, a, b);
  return getSum(node.left) + node.key * node.cnt + rangeSum(node.right, a, b);
}
```

